  "name": "Example: Calculating the Dot Product Using the General Formula",
  "problem": "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 0,-0.4,11 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,5,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 2+(-0.4)\\cdot 5+11\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0-2+22 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
